---
name: ask_owner
version: 1
permission: mutate
side_effecting: true
params:
  type: object
  properties:
    question:
      type: string
      description: The one question, in one sentence, naming the specific thing you cannot settle from the note — "Which Sarah is this, your sister or Sarah Chen from work?", not "Can you tell me more about this note?".
  required: [question]
---
Record ONE question about this note for Jeff and stop. Use it for the bar your
instructions already set: two people in the note share a name and nothing in it tells
them apart, or the meaning turns on a date the note never gives. Not to have a reading
approved, not for anything the note answers on a second read, and not as a hedge — you
commit your reading and Jeff corrects you by replying, so a question you did not need
costs more than a wrong link would. Anything you CAN settle, settle and write first.

Calling this ENDS YOUR TURN. Nothing you were going to do after it happens, so do the
writing first and ask last, in that order, in the same turn. What you already wrote
stands.

The note then waits on Jeff — there is no nagging and no deadline, and nothing else runs
over this note until he answers. When he does, his answer is appended to the note as a
dated clarification (it becomes part of the note's text, so it is a source like the rest
of the note), the note is re-read from scratch, and you take up the thread with the full
tool set.

Ask once. A second question in the same turn is refused: the first one already ended it.
